  "problem": "Consider the equation ${x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+20{x}^{2}-64x+64=0.$ Given that $x=2$ is a solution of multiplicity $2,$ find the remaining solutions in the form $\\pm b\\,\\text{i},$ where $b$ is **non-negative** number.\n\n$x=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}$\\text{i}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+20{x}^{2}-64x+64.$ Since ${x}_{1,2}=2$ is a root of multiplicity $2,$ according to the factor theorem, \n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}={x}^{2}-4x+4\n$$\n\nis a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nNow, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-4x+4$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+16 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-4x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+20{x}^{2}-64x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,16{x}^{2}-64x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{16{x}^{2}-64x+64}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}+16).$\n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve ${x}^{2}+16=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the remaining solutions to our original equation, apart from ${x}_{1,2}=2,$ are $x=\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}.$",
